  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Madrasso. Type: Partnership trick-taking. Target: 777 points. Deck: 40-card Italian. Rules: Follow suit, must overtake, trump if void. Card values: Ace=11, 3=10, King=4, Knight=3, Jack=2. Last trick=10 points. Can exchange 7 of trumps for indicator.',
    Player: 'Welcome to Madrasso. Partner with your teammate to reach 777 points before your opponents. Watch for the trump indicatorâ€”you may be able to exchange your 7 for a better card. Remember: follow suit, overtake when possible, and track those valuable Aces and 3s!',
    objective: 'Win the game by being the first partnership to reach 777 points over at least 10 deals (battute), counting points from tricks and the 10-point bonus for the last trick; or win immediately by taking all 10 tricks in one deal (cappotto).',
    gameplay: '1. Must follow suit if possible. 2. If void, you can play a trump or discard any card. 3. The highest card of the led suit wins, unless a trump is played (Highest trump wins). 4. Winner of trick leads next.',
